# Bug Report

There is a PR #44048 with a fix & test case for this, but it breaks two other tests.

Edited: Made a more minimal and thorough test case.

The TypeScript emitter incorrectly attaches comments into inside of syntesized lists since it thinks the comment after the newly synthesized list should be after the last element of the list. This might not appear anywhere else since I'm not sure if any other code creates such lists in a similar way in transformers like my Pipeline operator experiment for TypeScript.

I do have a fix for this for my issue, but then two existings tests fail. This feels like it could be a bigger bug and my fix is rather specific. .

The minimal case transformer just wraps function calls into a commalist. The transformer also wraps the expression into parens, but it's mainly to make the bug more apparent - the bug happens even without it.
```ts
function wrapInCommaList(context: TransformationContext) {
    return (sourceFile: SourceFile): SourceFile => {
        return visitNode(sourceFile, rootTransform, isSourceFile);
    };
    function rootTransform<T extends Node>(node: T): Node {
        if (isIdentifier(node) || isCallExpression(node)) {
            return factory.createParenthesizedExpression(
                factory.createCommaListExpression([
                    node
                ])
            );
        }
        return visitEachChild(node, rootTransform, context);
    }
}
```

This seems to happen in really specific situations. This bug won't occur if I manually create the same AST shape manually in the transformer that haven't had their pos, end, flags and parents set. Going to investigate this more.

